ALVA — Home Screen Grammar and Capitalization Fix

Objective

Review and correct all spelling, grammar, punctuation, and capitalization inconsistencies on the Home Screen only of ALVA.

The goal is to make every user-facing Home Screen label grammatically correct, polished, professional, and consistent.

This is strictly a text-correction update, not a redesign or gameplay update.

Repository context

Repository: hiyroscript/alva

ALVA is a browser-based 2D platform fighting game built with HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.

The Home Screen provides access to:

* Play — starts the battle setup flow.
* Watch Mode — allows players to watch CPU-versus-CPU battles.
* Practice Ground — opens the training environment.
* Discover — opens the game’s reference information.
* Settings — opens the settings dialog.
* Credits — displays the scrolling contributor and attribution information.

The interface supports English and French through a localization system.

Relevant source files

Inspect these files before implementing any changes:

* js/screens/home-screen.js — Home Screen structure and navigation.
* js/localization/strings/en.js — English interface strings.
* js/localization/strings/fr.js — French interface strings.
* js/localization/i18n.js — Translation and localization behavior.
* js/ui/credits.js — Home Screen credits content.
* css/home.css — Home Screen styling and responsiveness.
* tests/interface/i18n.test.mjs — Localization tests.

Follow the repository’s existing conventions and architecture.

1. Apply consistent capitalization

Use sentence case for Home Screen buttons and labels.

Sentence case means capitalizing the first word and proper nouns, rather than capitalizing every word.

Required English corrections

Current wording	Corrected wording
Watch Mode	Watch mode
Practice Ground	Practice ground
Play	Play
Discover	Discover
Settings	Settings
Credits	Credits

The last four examples are already correct and should remain unchanged.

Apply the first two corrections specifically to the Home Screen’s localization keys:

* home.watch: Watch mode
* home.practice: Practice ground

Do not change setup.watch, screen.practice, or any other strings belonging to different screens.

French consistency

Apply the equivalent sentence-case convention where appropriate.

For example:

* home.watch: Mode Spectateur → Mode spectateur

Keep existing French translations that are already grammatically correct.

Follow French capitalization and punctuation conventions rather than mechanically applying English rules.

2. Audit all Home Screen text

Review every piece of text rendered directly on the Home Screen, including:

* Navigation buttons
* The introductory tagline
* Credits headings and descriptions
* Contributor attribution
* Footer text
* Settings button tooltip and accessible name
* Accessibility labels and instructions
* Empty-roster messages
* Any other text that appears specifically on Home

Check for:

1. Incorrect capitalization
2. Spelling errors
3. Grammar mistakes
4. Missing or unnecessary punctuation
5. Inconsistent terminology
6. Awkward phrasing that reduces clarity

Keep corrections minimal. Preserve the original meaning, tone, and personality of ALVA.

The tagline Fan project. Big heart. is intentionally short and expressive. Do not rewrite it simply because it uses sentence fragments.

Preserve proper nouns such as ALVA, DeviantArt, contributor names, character identifiers, and developer names.

3. Review Home Screen credits

The Home Screen includes scrolling credits populated from js/ui/credits.js and the localization dictionaries.

Review the credits for grammatical accuracy and consistency.

In particular, inspect the English credits.original.line text and consider replacing the awkward Desert / City stage artwork phrasing with natural wording such as Desert and City stage artwork.

Maintain all original attribution information and legal meaning.

Do not remove, rename, or alter contributor identities, source links, or ownership acknowledgments.

If French credits require corresponding grammatical corrections, update those translations accurately.

4. Improve accessibility text when necessary

The Home Screen includes accessibility descriptions such as:

Credits. Scroll or use arrow and Page keys to read.

Review these instructions for clarity and grammatical correctness.

A clearer English alternative would be:

Credits. Scroll or use the arrow keys, Page Up, and Page Down to read.

Verify the actual supported keyboard interactions before changing any instructions.

Ensure screen readers receive accurate labels and that language switching continues to update accessibility text correctly.

5. Respect the Home Screen boundary

CRITICAL: Only modify text displayed on the Home Screen.

Do not make grammar or capitalization corrections elsewhere, even if similar inconsistencies exist.

Specifically, do not change:

* Battle screens or gameplay HUD
* Watch mode setup screens
* Practice ground gameplay
* Discover pages
* Settings dialog contents
* Character selection
* Difficulty selection
* Stage selection
* Loading screens
* Game mechanics or character data
* General documentation or unrelated localization entries

The Settings button’s Home Screen tooltip is in scope, but the Settings dialog itself is not.

If a translation key is shared between Home and another screen, do not change its global wording if doing so would affect another screen. Use an existing Home-specific key or introduce a narrowly scoped one only when necessary.

Do not perform a repository-wide capitalization replacement.

6. Preserve the existing interface

No visual redesign is permitted.

Keep the following completely unchanged:

* Home Screen layout and structure
* ALVA logo and branding
* Fonts, typography, and font sizes
* Colors, backgrounds, and borders
* Button placement and dimensions
* Spacing and alignment
* Animations and transitions
* Scrolling credits behavior
* Responsive layouts
* Keyboard, mouse, touch, and gamepad navigation
* Button functionality and navigation destinations

Text corrections must not introduce clipping, overflow, or unnecessary line wrapping.

Avoid CSS or component changes unless absolutely required to display the corrected text properly.

7. Preserve localization functionality

English and French must continue working correctly.

Do not rename existing translation keys unnecessarily.

Preserve interpolation placeholders such as {developer} and {title}.

Ensure that switching languages updates Home Screen text immediately, without requiring a reload.

Do not introduce hardcoded text directly into the Home Screen component when the localization system should own that text.

8. Validation and testing

After making the corrections:

1. Verify every visible Home Screen label in English.
2. Verify the French translations.
3. Check the credits and footer.
4. Confirm accessibility descriptions are accurate.
5. Verify that all four primary navigation buttons still work.
6. Confirm the Settings button still opens the Settings dialog.
7. Confirm the credits still scroll and their links still work.
8. Check desktop and mobile landscape layouts.
9. Confirm no other game’s screens have changed.

Run the relevant existing tests:

node --test tests/interface/i18n.test.mjs

Then run the full test suite:

node --test

Add focused tests where useful to verify the corrected Home Screen wording and prevent capitalization regressions.

Do not unnecessarily rewrite existing tests.

9. Deliverables

Provide a concise final report containing:

* Every Home Screen string corrected
* Its previous wording
* Its corrected wording
* The modified files
* Any remaining text intentionally preserved
* Test results
* Confirmation that no other screen was modified

Final acceptance criteria

The update is complete when:

* Watch Mode displays as Watch mode on Home.
* Practice Ground displays as Practice ground on Home.
* All other Home Screen wording has been audited for actual grammatical issues.
* English and French remain consistent and correct.
* Credits and accessibility labels are grammatically sound.
* The Home Screen looks and functions exactly as before.
* No other screen or gameplay system has been changed.

Final instruction: Make the smallest possible set of changes. This task is exclusively about improving Home Screen text quality, capitalization, and grammatical consistency. Do not expand its scope.
